{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"The alternative-library sweep found a meaningful gain only for the large `grad_weight` projection: its best fixed hipBLASLt algorithm is roughly 25–30% faster than PyTorch’s selected one at `N=8192`. I’m tuning that one projection over representative sizes; the exact Triton front end and the safer PyTorch path remain unchanged until the replacement proves correct across every workload."}}
