{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"The tuned forward-projection kernels are also numerically identical (or differ only by one BF16 ulp in a handful of elements). I’m enabling the best per-shape choices for that projection, and removing the `N=6144` weight-gradient override because the end-to-end evaluator showed PyTorch was faster there despite isolated measurements."}}
